SUMMARY:Deadline: Bellingcat Contractor: AI Engineer (Open Source Agentic S
 ystems)
DESCRIPTION:Bellingcat\, the open source investigations collective\, is hir
 ing a contractor AI engineer to build agentic systems that support its inv
 estigators.\n\nOrganisation: Bellingcat\nLocation: Remote. Requires a time
  zone with sufficient overlap with Bellingcat's Europe-based team.\nAward:
  Annual contractor fee of USD 80\,000 to 93\,000 for full-time (40 hours/w
 eek)\, depending on experience and track record\; a part-time (20 hours/we
 ek) option is also offered\, rate not stated.\nDuration: Initial 12-month 
 contract\, full-time or part-time\, starting as soon as possible.\n\nMore:
  https://www.bellingcat.com/contractor-ai-engineer-open-source-agentic-sys
 tems/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bellingcat.com/contractor-ai-engineer-open-source-agentic-s
 ystems/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote. Requires a time zone with sufficient overlap with Bellingc
 at's Europe-based team.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mozilla-incubator-human-scale-ai-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T234826Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mozilla Foundation Incubator: Human-Scale AI cohort 2027 
 (call for proposals)
DESCRIPTION:The Mozilla Foundation Incubator's next cohort funds seven Huma
 n-Scale AI projects: working AI technologies that are small (small models\
 , less compute\, able to run locally or on low-power devices)\, intentiona
 l (users and communities get insight into and control over their data\, an
 d systems can be configured\, forked or community-governed) and tailored (
 fit-for-purpose for a specific community\,...\n\nOrganisation: Mozilla Fou
 ndation (Mozilla Foundation Incubator)\nLocation: Remote cohort worldwide\
 , with a platform at the Mozilla Festival.\nAward: USD 300\,000 non-diluti
 ve funding plus 12 months of support for each of seven selected projects\;
  projects showing strong progress may receive up to USD 200\,000 more and 
 two further years of support\, for a total of up to USD 500\,000 over thre
 e years. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months from April 2027\, with p
 ossible follow-on support for two more years.\n\nMore: https://www.mozilla
 foundation.org/en/what-we-do/grantmaking/incubator/human-scale-ai/call-for
 -proposals/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mozillafoundation.org/en/what-we-do/grantmaking/incubator/h
 uman-scale-ai/call-for-proposals/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote cohort worldwide\, with a platform at the Mozilla Festival.
END:VEVENT
