SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute: AI for Science and Safety Nodes RFP 
 2026 (Local Compute\; Coordination and Accountability\; AI-first Science)
DESCRIPTION:Foresight Institute's AI for Science and Safety Nodes request f
 or proposals funds open\, AI-first projects across three calls: I. Local C
 ompute (compute that individuals and communities physically own and contro
 l)\, II.\n\nOrganisation: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Remote-friendly w
 orldwide\; optional in-person membership at the Foresight AI Nodes in San 
 Francisco or Berlin.\nAward: Grants typically USD 30\,000 to 100\,000 (sma
 ller awards for the Human Empowerment and AI Insurance and Open Governance
  areas\, larger for the rest\; bigger amounts possible for the right proje
 ct)\, usually paid as one lump sum\, with up to 10 percent overhead. Optio
 nal office space in San Francisco or Berlin and access to private compute 
 clusters. No application fee.\nDuration: Short-term and multi-year project
 s\; larger multi-year grants are paid in milestone tranches.\n\nMore: http
 s://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote-friendly worldwide\; optional in-person membership at the F
 oresight AI Nodes in San Francisco or Berlin.
END:VEVENT
